# Tooling

Summary: Shared tools and command conventions. A project's `tools.md` defines its exact invocations and wins over these defaults.

## za

- `za` is the canonical command for managing this workspace's architecture.
- It replaces hand-written management scripts: never add shell, Python or Make scripts under `.agents/` that duplicate workspace-management behavior.
- Available: `za init`, already applied to this workspace.
- Until a `za` subcommand covers a task (adding a project, checking drift, creating or removing worktrees), perform it with the native tools below, following `policy.md`.

## Native tools

Native tools are used directly; their behavior is never emulated by hand.

| Tool | Role in this workspace |
|---|---|
| `git` | Repository, submodule (`.gitmodules`, gitlinks) and worktree mechanism. |
| `go` | Go toolchain. Owns root `go.work` and `go.work.sum`; change membership with `go work use`. |

## Conventions

- Run commands directly with explicit arguments and working directories.
- Prefer project-owned entry points (scripts, Make/Task targets, CI-equivalent commands) documented in project `tools.md` over reconstructed command lines.
- Every documented command states its mode: `standalone` or `workspace`.
- Go standalone commands in task worktrees set `GOWORK=off`; see `go-standards.md`.
- Capabilities a project requires (OpenSpec CLI, agent skills, plugins) are listed in its `tools.md`.

## Project context templates

`templates/project/` is the single scaffold source for new project contexts. Placeholders state who supplies each value:

| Placeholder | Supplied by |
|---|---|
| `<project-id>`, `<full-submodule-SHA>`, `YYYY-MM-DD` | Structure: known when the project is added. |
| `<discover: ...>` | Inspection of the public repository (paths, commands, runtime). |
| `<decide: ...>` | A human decision (summary, constraints, decisions, plans). |

Never replace a placeholder with an invented fact. Use `not applicable` when a row does not apply.
